== JWT signing key strength

HMAC JWTs rely on a secret key to sign and verify tokens. A short or predictable key can be recovered
with an offline dictionary attack, allowing an attacker to forge claims.

=== Assignment

The sample token is signed with a random 256-bit key generated by the server. Try changing its claims
and observe that the signature check rejects the modified token. A key with this much entropy cannot
be recovered with a practical dictionary attack. Production signing keys should be managed outside
source code and rotated through trusted configuration.
